# Zoom speaking notes

When the user asks for a **script**, talking points, what to say, or notes for a
hearing / CMC / Zoom appearance:

- Follow `.claude/skills/hearing-script/SKILL.md`.
- Render it **in the chat**.
- **Bold** lines always start with `(don't say)` — stage directions, never spoken.
- Regular type is the only read-aloud. Short complete sentences. His voice. Sounds smart, not like a brief.
- Never use "If they say…", "Q. / A.", "Point A", or "Read this" — those get spoken by accident.
- Skip-blocks behind bold gates, not a six-page PDF.

Locked after the August 28, 2026 CHP demurrer (Matter 20). The Court could tell when heading and speech were the same type.
